hotel","la":42.35666,"lo":-71.050316,"d":2049,"w":"https://www.bostonharborhotel.com/","ph":"+1 617 439 7000","wifi":1,"ds":"The Boston Harbor Hotel is a luxury hotel overlooking Boston Harbor and the Rose Kennedy Greenway. It is a member of Preferred Hotels & Resorts Worldwide. The hotel is the principal occupant of the Rowes Wharf building, completed in 1987, and designed by Adrian Smith while he was working for Skidmore, Owings and Merrill (SOM).","wpu":"Boston Harbor Hotel","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Boston_Harbor_Hotel_%2854959755872%29.jpg/960px-Boston_Harbor_Hotel_%2854959755872%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Washington Monument","g":"sights","k":"monument","la":42.353758,"lo":-71.053982,"d":2124},{"n":"New England Aquarium Whale Watching","g":"sights","k":"attraction","la":42.359385,"lo":-71.049992,"d":2234},{"n":"Alexander Graham Bell Room Museum","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":42.355587,"lo":-71.055111,"d":2304},{"n":"Boston Marriott Long Wharf","g":"sights","k":"hotel","la":42.360183,"lo":-71.050852,"d":2347,"h":"24/7","w":"https://www.marriott.com/hotels/travel/boslw-boston-marriott-long-wharf/","ph":"+1-617-227-0800","wifi":1},{"n":"Custom House Tower Observation Deck","g":"sights","k":"viewpoint","la":42.359008,"lo":-71.053501,"d":2417},{"n":"Marriott Vacation Club Pulse® at Custom House","g":"sights","k":"hotel","la":42.35908,"lo":-71.05365,"d":2432,"w":"https://www.marriott.com/hotels/travel/bosch-marriott-vacation-club-pulse-at-custom-house-boston/","ph":"+1-617-310-6300","wifi":1},{"n":"Ancient and Honorable Artillery Company Museum","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":42.360113,"lo":-71.056119,"d":2661,"h":"Mo-Fr 09:00-15:00","w":"http://www.ahac.us.com/","ph":"+1-617-227-1638","wp":"en:Ancient and Honorable Artillery Company of Massachusetts","ds":"The Ancient and Honorable Artillery Company of Massachusetts is the oldest chartered military organization in North America and the third oldest chartered military organization in the world. A volunteer militia of the Commonwealth of Massachusetts, it is not part of the U.S. Armed Forces, but includes veterans and serving military members within its ranks.","wpu":"Ancient and Honorable Artillery Company of Massachusetts","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Arms_of_the_Ancient_and_Honorable_Artillery_Company_of_Massachusetts.png/960px-Arms_of_the_Ancient_and_Honorable_Artillery_Company_of_Massachusetts.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"ClipArt Gallery","g":"sights","k":"gallery","la":42.367672,"lo":-71.042225,"d":2684,"h":"Sa 12:00-16:00"},{"n":"Samuel Adams","g":"sights","k":"artwork","la":42.359982,"lo":-71.056772,"d":2694,"wp":"en:Statue of Samuel Adams","ds":"Anne Whitney created two public statues of American Founding Father Samuel Adams. One, made in 1876, is in the National Statuary Hall Collection in the United States Capitol, Washington, D.C. The other, made in 1880, is located in front of Faneuil Hall Plaza in Boston.","wpu":"Statue of Samuel Adams","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Flickr_-_USCapitol_-_Samuel_Adams_Statue.jpg/960px-Flickr_-_USCapitol_-_Samuel_Adams_Statue.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Josiah Quincy III","g":"sights","k":"monument","la":42.357852,"lo":-71.059356,"d":2733},{"n":"Benjamin Franklin Statue","g":"sights","k":"monument","la":42.357933,"lo":-71.059568,"d":2753},{"n":"Pierce/Hichborn House Museum","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":42.363531,"lo":-71.053768,"d":2783,"w":"https://www.paulreverehouse.org/pierce-hichborn-house/"},{"n":"First Public School Site","g":"sights","k":"attraction","la":42.358014,"lo":-71.060007,"d":2788,"w":"https://www.thefreedomtrail.org/trail-sites/boston-latin-school-sitebenjamin-franklin-statue"},{"n":"Stop & Shop","g":"essentials","k":"supermarket","la":42.335479,"lo":-71.